# PR fast-check receipt manifest (goal item 4/5).
#
# Read by scripts/check/sign-local-ci-receipt.shs and
# scripts/check/verify-local-ci-receipt.shs through
# SIMPLE_CI_RECEIPT_MANIFEST_REL=config/check/pr_fast_gates.sdn, so a
# `pr`-tier receipt binds exactly this one row. It is a separate file only
# because config/check/must_check_gates.sdn is owned by another lane; the
# intended end state is this row folded into that manifest by its owner.
#
# The row command is what scripts/check/check-pr-fast.shs --sign-key ... runs;
# the signer is fed --results from that run, never --run, because the command
# needs the PR range.
must_check_gates |id, tier, push_blocking, mode, command, ci_job, inputs, description|
    pr-fast-changed, pr, false, range, "sh scripts/check/check-pr-fast.shs --range", pr-fast-check, -, "changed .spl files compile (syntax-only by default; callers in unchanged files and deleted files are NOT compiled), their unit specs and their feature (03_system) specs run, all inside a 60s budget. The signed receipt additionally binds compile mode, budget and the simple binary's size+sha256 in its session_id field (see sign_receipt() in check-pr-fast.shs), captured once at process start (not after the run, to close a TOCTOU on a redeployed binary); the remote verify_receipt() rejects a receipt missing that binding AND rejects one binding a budget over 60s (MAX_ACCEPTED_BUDGET). The binary hash is disclosed, not checked against an allowlist — see verify_receipt()'s comment for why a committed allowlist of binary hashes was rejected as impractical. Before signing, the working tree is also checked for gitignored .spl sitting alongside tracked .spl (a directory a change adds to gitignore's build/ pattern without also carving out a negation), since those are invisible to the untracked-file check but importable locally."
